{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2310,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have made your prediction and now it is\ntime to see what happens when I release the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6210,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "balance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7240,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ready?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8280,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In three, two, one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13990,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The balance tips towards the right, towards\nthe hanging, heavier ball."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19150,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why does this happen?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21570,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the best way I can think of to explain\nthis is that both balls displace the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26640,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amount of water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28070,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they both experience the same upward buoyant\nforce which is equal to the weight of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33030,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "water they displace."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34030,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is just Archimedes Principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36090,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But by Newton’s Third Law, that means there\nmust be equal and opposite forces down on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40820,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the water in both beakers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42650,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you would think that both beakers would\nget heavier by this same amount."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47220,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now for the hanging ball the beaker does get\nheavier by this amount, because the buoyant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51260,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "force is now supporting some of the weight\nthat used to be supported by this tension"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55690,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the string."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56690,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it is now reduced and so beaker actually\nhas more weight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60610,
    "dDurationMs": 5649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for the ping pong ball, the downward force\non the water is almost entirely counteracted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66259,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the upward force of the tension in that\nstring on the bottom of the beaker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70619,
    "dDurationMs": 4081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, therefore, the weight of this beaker\nonly increases by the weight of the ping pong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74700,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ball itself, whereas for the hanging ball\nthe weight increases by the weight of water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79520,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it displaces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81270,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So obviously this beaker is going to end up\nbeing heavier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84899,
    "dDurationMs": 2650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I want to propose an additional experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87549,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if instead of tethering the ping pong\nball to the base of this beaker, I just got"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91749,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a free ping pong ball and submerged it with\nmy finger, just barely under the surface of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96869,
    "dDurationMs": 1001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the water?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97870,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that case, what do you think would happen\nwhen the scale was allowed to rotate?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102009,
    "dDurationMs": 5441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would it tilt down A) towards the hanging\nacrylic ball or B)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107450,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down towards the ping pong ball, which is\nnow just barely submerged under the water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110920,
    "dDurationMs": 7939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or C) would the balance remain perfectly balanced?So\nI want you to make your selection, make your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118859,
    "dDurationMs": 5711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prediction by leaving a comment starting with\neither A, B or C and then giving me your explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124570,
    "dDurationMs": 6940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I will tally up the votes and let you\nknow the answer next time."
    } ]
  } ]
}
